   "customer_impact": "Customers lose time, money (advance payments, fees, repair costs) and trust, and describe repeated chasing with no owner. Several state they have escalated outside the app (consumer forums, legal notice).",
   "connection_to_repeat_booking": "Recourse is the strongest differentiator among customers who state or signal what they will do: 40.0% of those 310 Non-Return reviews cite recourse failures against 4.0% of the 548 Return reviews. A reading of the evidence, not proof of cause.",
   "why_it_matters_to_urban_company": "A single failed booking is recoverable if resolution is quick; the evidence suggests that the resolution experience, more than the original failure, shapes whether customers describe leaving.",
